 "text": "Hey, how are you doing these days? The app Duolingo is the champion, with each five-minute lesson taking only a few minutes. You can go through it on the subway, or while waiting for coffee. Follow a list first, then do few random words to get used the card flips, then flip a lot at once. Lots of apps do this, Duolingo is the most fun. Stick to simple readers, like The Goodbye Girl or Harris's Moon On Your Boot for A1 A2. Pick a few words you' mispronounce. Lots of elementary readers do, and they' great for confidence.",
